  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "2002 (Jun. -Jul.) U.S. Echo Integration-trawl Survey Data for Walleye Pollock (Theragra chalcogramma) on the Bering Sea Shelf and Slope (Cruise ID: MF0002-08)",
  "description": "Echo integration-trawl (EIT) survey was carried out between 4 June and 30 July 2002 on the eastern Berign Sea (EBS) shelf. Sampled data include pollock distribution, relative abundance, size composition and maturity, acoustic data, and oceanographic data of temperature/depth profiles, conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) profiles, sea surface temperature and salinity, and ocean current profile. This survey was conducted in cooperation with the research vessel TINRO from TINRO Centre, Vladivostok, Russia. Cruise ID: MF0002-08 (June 4 - July 30, 2002) Survey vessel: NOAA ship R/V Miller Freeman For cruise results see http://www.afsc.noaa.gov/race/surveys/cruise_archives/cruises2002/rsltsMF2002-08.pdf\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect echo integration and trawl data to estimate midwater pollock abundance and distribution.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23513793",
